I now have a complete picture. Here's the full report.

## 1. Computation site

**`storepb.MemoPayload` definition** — `/bench/home/work/proto/store/memo.proto:7-29`
```proto
message MemoPayload {
  Property property = 1;
  Location location = 2;
  repeated string tags = 3;

  message Property {
    bool has_link = 1;
    bool has_task_list = 2;
    bool has_code = 3;
    bool has_incomplete_tasks = 4;
    string title = 5;   // extracted from the first H1 heading, if present
  }

  message Location {
    string placeholder = 1;
    double latitude = 2;
    double longitude = 3;
  }
}
```
Generated Go structs in `/bench/home/work/proto/gen/store/memo.pb.go:24-31` (`MemoPayload`: `Property`, `Location`, `Tags []string`) and `:85-95` (`MemoPayload_Property`: `HasLink`, `HasTaskList`, `HasCode`, `HasIncompleteTasks`, `Title`). Note `Location` has no extraction — it's set manually from client-supplied request data (`convertLocationToStore`), not derived from content.

**`RebuildMemoPayload`** — `/bench/home/work/server/runner/memopayload/runner.go:74-88`
```go
func RebuildMemoPayload(_ context.Context, memo *store.Memo, markdownService markdown.Service) error {
    if memo.Payload == nil {
        memo.Payload = &storepb.MemoPayload{}
    }
    // Use goldmark service to extract all metadata in a single pass (more efficient)
    data, err := markdownService.ExtractAll([]byte(memo.Content))
    if err != nil {
        return errors.Wrap(err, "failed to extract markdown metadata")
    }
    memo.Payload.Tags = data.Tags
    memo.Payload.Property = data.Property
    return nil
}
```
Steps: (1) lazily init `memo.Payload` if nil; (2) call `markdownService.ExtractAll(content)` — a single-pass goldmark AST walk that parses the markdown once; (3) overwrite `memo.Payload.Tags` with `data.Tags` and `memo.Payload.Property` with `data.Property`. It does **not** touch `memo.Payload.Location` (that field is preserved/set elsewhere).

Note: `runner.go` also defines a `Runner` type with `RunOnce` (`:14-72`) that batch-reprocesses all memos 100 at a time, calling `RebuildMemoPayload` then `Store.UpdateMemo`. However, this `Runner`/`RunOnce` is **not currently wired up** in `/bench/home/work/server/server.go` — `startBackgroundRunners` (`server.go:153-173`) only starts the `s3presign` runner; there is no `memopayload.NewRunner(...)` call anywhere in the codebase (confirmed via repo-wide grep — only `runner.go` itself and `memo_service.go`'s two `RebuildMemoPayload` calls reference the `memopayload` package). So today the payload is only rebuilt inline during Create/Update RPCs, not via a background job.

**`ExtractAll`** — `/bench/home/work/internal/markdown/markdown.go:356-422`, and the `Service` interface at `:31-55`. It parses content once (`s.parse`, line 356-360) and does a single `gast.Walk`:
- Tag nodes (`asMemoTagNode`, filtering out tags inside links/images) → `data.Tags` (lines 376-378)
- Mention nodes (`*mast.MentionNode`) → `data.Mentions`, lowercased (lines 379-381)
- If the first block-level child of the document is an H1 heading → `data.Property.Title` (lines 383-389, via `extractHeadingText`)
- `gast.KindLink` → `data.Property.HasLink = true` (lines 392-394)
- `gast.KindCodeBlock`, `KindFencedCodeBlock`, `KindCodeSpan` → `data.Property.HasCode = true` (lines 396-397)
- `east.KindTaskCheckBox` → `data.Property.HasTaskList = true`, and if unchecked → `data.Property.HasIncompleteTasks = true` (lines 399-405)

Finally tags/mentions are deduplicated (case-preserving) via `uniquePreserveCase` (lines 417-419, 455-468).

`ExtractedData` struct (`markdown.go:21-25`):
```go
type ExtractedData struct {
    Tags     []string
    Mentions []string
    Property *storepb.MemoPayload_Property
}
```
Note `Mentions` is extracted but is **not** persisted into `MemoPayload` — it's only used transiently (see part 2 below) for mention-notification resolution, not stored as derived metadata on the memo.

There are also standalone `ExtractTags` (`:143-170`) and `ExtractProperties` (`:193-241`) methods that duplicate the same logic individually (each does its own `gast.Walk`), but `RebuildMemoPayload` uses only the combined `ExtractAll`.

## 2. RPC handlers that trigger recomputation

Both call sites are in `/bench/home/work/server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go`:

- **`CreateMemo`** — line 108: `if err := memopayload.RebuildMemoPayload(ctx, create, s.MarkdownService); err != nil { ... }` (function starts at line 70). Always runs on every memo creation, right after content-length validation (lines 101-107) and before `s.Store.CreateMemo` (line 115). Immediately after (lines 111-113), `create.Payload.Location` is separately populated from `request.Memo.Location` if provided — confirming `RebuildMemoPayload` doesn't touch Location.

- **`UpdateMemo`** — line 447, inside the `for _, path := range request.UpdateMask.Paths` loop (function starts at line 401), specifically in the `path == "content"` branch (lines 436-451):
```go
if path == "content" {
    contentUpdated = true
    previousContent = memo.Content
    ... length check ...
    memo.Content = request.Memo.Content
    if err := memopayload.RebuildMemoPayload(ctx, memo, s.MarkdownService); err != nil {
        return nil, status.Errorf(codes.Internal, "failed to rebuild memo payload: %v", err)
    }
    update.Content = &memo.Content
    update.Payload = memo.Payload
}
```
So recomputation only happens **when the update mask includes `"content"`** (i.e., the caller is actually changing the memo body). Other update-mask paths (`visibility`, `pinned`, `state`, `create_time`, `update_time`, `location`, `attachments`, `relations`, etc.) do not trigger payload recomputation; the `location` path (lines 481-484) mutates `update.Payload.Location` directly without touching `Property`/`Tags`.

`previousContent`/`contentUpdated` (lines 433-434, 438) are captured for downstream logic (e.g., tag-rename propagation, mention-diff notification dispatch) elsewhere in the same function — not part of payload computation itself, but confirm the recompute is scoped to actual content edits.

## 3. Exactly what gets extracted

From `storepb.MemoPayload` populated by `RebuildMemoPayload`/`ExtractAll`:
- **`Tags []string`** — all `#tag` occurrences in the markdown, deduplicated case-preserving, excluding tags that appear inside links/images (`isTagNodeInLinkOrImage`, `markdown.go:122-140`)
- **`Property.HasLink bool`** — true if any `gast.KindLink` node exists
- **`Property.HasCode bool`** — true if any code block, fenced code block, or inline code span exists
- **`Property.HasTaskList bool`** — true if any GFM task checkbox (`- [ ]`/`- [x]`) exists
- **`Property.HasIncompleteTasks bool`** — true if at least one task checkbox is unchecked
- **`Property.Title string`** — text of the first H1 heading, only if it is the very first block-level element in the document

Extracted but **not** stored in `MemoPayload` (used only transiently):
- **`Mentions []string`** — `@username` mentions, lowercased/deduped, computed by the same `ExtractAll` call but consumed separately by `resolveMentionTargets` in `/bench/home/work/server/router/api/v1/memo_mention_helpers.go:26-54` (used to look up users to notify, called from `dispatchMemoMentionNotificationsBestEffort`, not persisted on the memo payload)
- **Snippet** — `GenerateSnippet(content, maxLength)` (`markdown.go:264-346`) is a separate extraction method producing a plain-text summary; it is used only for webhook payloads (`/bench/home/work/server/router/api/v1/memo_service_webhooks.go:85`, `snippet, err := s.MarkdownService.GenerateSnippet([]byte(content), 64)`) and is **not** stored in `storepb.MemoPayload` at all — there's no `Snippet` field in the proto.

There is no `has_todo` field (only `has_task_list` + `has_incomplete_tasks`) and no "references" extraction field in the current proto, despite the `ExtractAll` doc comment (`markdown.go:32`) mentioning "references in a single parse" — that appears aspirational/stale, since no reference data is produced or stored today.
